sharprs-core NOTICE
===================

sharprs-core is an independent Rust implementation of the sounding
analysis algorithms of SHARPpy (https://github.com/sharppy/SHARPpy), which
were used as the numerical reference. No SHARPpy source code is included.

The following data files are distributed with this crate unmodified:

  data/sars_hail.txt, data/sars_supercell.txt
      SARS (Sounding Analog Retrieval System) hail and supercell analog
      databases by R. Thompson, J. Hart et al. (NOAA/NWS Storm Prediction
      Center). Created by US federal government employees as part of their
      duties (17 U.S.C. 105) and therefore in the public domain; obtained
      via SHARPpy.

  data/PW-mean-inches.txt, data/PW-stdev-inches.txt
